  "name": "TrustDemoOnesaImmunization",
  "title": "Onesa: dose on the national schedule",
  "status": "draft",
  "description": "How it is used: J3 and after. These are the Taifafeki birth doses once the district clinic has verified them, and every dose given in Onesa.\n\nWhy: the Onesan schedule engine works on Onesan EPI codes, so each dose must carry one. A dose that came from abroad keeps the issuer's product code beside the Onesan one, added through the ConceptMap and confirmed by the nurse. Nothing the other country said is overwritten. A verified foreign dose is recorded from its primary source, the signing hospital, and its Provenance says how it was verified.",
  "fhirVersion": "4.0.1",
  "kind": "resource",
  "abstract": false,
  "type": "Immunization",
